set group id is enough for nethack.

On my box,  nethack is installed under
lib/nethackdir
except for a frontend binary.

lib/nethackdir/ 	is mode 0775
lib/nethackdir/logfile 	is mode 0664
lib/nethackdir/nethack	is mode 2555 (so that's the setgid binary)
lib/nethackdir/perm	is mode 0664
lib/nethackdir/record	is mode 0664
lib/nethackdir/save/	is mode 0575

and that's enough for a standard installation here. No need to be root.
In fact, my nethack is just setgid games.

If I recall things right, the only user hardcoded within the games is
the wizard, so unless you want to play in wizard mode, you should be
safe.

The setgid part means those friends won't be able to use your account
even if a hole is found in  nethack (always a possibility, though unlikely
after so many years), they'll just be able to be in the same user group as
you.


